ership, but regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. Need to weigh.\n\nProbably best candidate is B? But nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. D has hot temper and know-it-all, also bad. C has communication issues, egocentric. A has show-off, not open to new ideas. All have concerns. Which is least concerning? B's nasty remarks could affect crew cooperation heavily. D's hot temper also. C's communication difficulty also. A's show-off maybe less severe? But not open to new ideas could affect adaptability. Might pick Candidate A as best overall: strong technical competence (anticipate dangerous, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership) and no explicit stress resilience note but maybe okay. No mention of memory issues or temperament. Concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas. Those are concerns but maybe less safety-critical than nasty remarks or hot temper. So I will recommend Candidate A.\n\nMake contribution: \"I think Candidate A is strongest overall because of technical competence and leadership, despite concerns about being a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas.\" Provide evidence.\n\nLet's produce."}
