y, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. D responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but arrogant, weak leadership. So we could argue that B has explicit stress handling evidence, but crew cooperation concerns. C has decision quality but communication issues. D has problem solving but arrogance.\n\nWe could propose that we need to gather data on stress resilience and crew cooperation for all candidates before final decision. But we need to give a recommendation now. Perhaps we can still vote for A but request data on others. Or we could shift to B because we have evidence of stress handling. But B also has uncooperative behavior. Which is more critical? Stress resilience is crucial for long-distance flights. Crew cooperation also crucial. A unknown on both. B known to handle stress well but uncooperative. C unknown stress, communication issues. D unknown stress, arrogance.\n\nThus maybe we should keep A as provisional but note we need data. So we can say we still recommend A but we need to probe stress and crew cooperation for all candidates. Provide a question to James or Emily for other candidates.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote. Vote remains Candidate A.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: agree with Emily, still recommend A, but highlight need for data on stress resilience and crew cooperation for all candidates, maybe ask James for B's crew cooperation, etc.\n\nWe must not include tool calls now, as we are just responding. The request is to handle as per system instruction, which we are doing.\n\nLet's craft concise message."}
